68	// `remember --branch <other>` files the fact on ANOTHER branch without moving
69	// the working tree, so HEAD is the wrong evidence: it is the CURRENT branch's
70	// tip, and it may not be on <other> at all. The stored fact then reads "on
71	// <other>, evidenced by <a commit that branch never had>" — and verification
72	// launders it, because verifyCommitUncached accepts reachability from ANY local
73	// ref rather than from the fact's branch.
